    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">疼痛，或伴有空虚感，喜揉喜按，揉按可使疼痛减轻。见于虚证、气虚证、气血两虚证等。又称疼痛喜揉按。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Pain or accompanied by an empty sensation fond of rubbing and pressing rubbing and pressing can relieve the pain. Seen in deficiency pattern; qi deficiency pattern; qi-blood dual deficiency pattern. Also known as pain relieved by rubbing and pressing.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.2.2.6</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:synonym>疼痛喜揉按</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:severityText>中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>每日多次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>寒冷刺激</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>休息、热敷</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:icd11>SE90</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Qi deficiency pattern (TM1)</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_疼痛喜按</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Pain or accompanied by an empty sensation fond of rubbing and pressing rubbing and pressing can relieve the pain. Seen in deficiency pattern; qi deficiency pattern; qi-blood dual deficiency pattern. Also known as pain relieved by rubbing and pressing.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>疼痛喜揉按</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ICD11:SE90</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
  </owl:Class>
