    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">脉体细小，其脉气来去连续无间断，故应指常有而不绝。见于阳虚证、血虚证、阴虚证等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">A thin, small pulse whose pulse qi comes and goes continuously without interruption, thus felt under the finger as persistent and unceasing. Seen in yang deficiency pattern, blood deficiency pattern, and yin deficiency pattern.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.2.2.9</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>每日多次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>感染、过敏</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>情绪调节</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:icd11>SF00</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Blood deficiency pattern (TM1)</tcm:icd11Term>
    <tcm:icd11>SR1T</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Blood deficiency pattern (TM2)</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_脉细</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A thin, small pulse whose pulse qi comes and goes continuously without interruption, thus felt under the finger as persistent and unceasing. Seen in yang deficiency pattern, blood deficiency pattern, and yin deficiency pattern.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ICD11:SF00</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ICD11:SR1T</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
