    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">如抚刀刃，浮之小急，按之坚大而急，见于肝之危候，肝肾阴竭。为无胃气之脉。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">A pulse like stroking a knife blade—slightly urgent on light pressure, firm, large and urgent on heavy pressure. Seen in critical liver conditions with exhaustion of liver-kidney yin; a pulse without stomach qi.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.2.2.20</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度至中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>间歇性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>受凉、劳累</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>药物治疗</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_偃刀脉</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A pulse like stroking a knife blade—slightly urgent on light pressure, firm, large and urgent on heavy pressure. Seen in critical liver conditions with exhaustion of liver-kidney yin; a pulse without stomach qi.</obo:IAO_0000115>
