    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/f#PsychiatricFinding"/>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">先血后便，或先便后血，或便血杂下，或单纯便血。见于肠风络伤证、肠道湿热证、肝肾阴虚证、脾肾阳虚证、脾虚气陷证、血热动血证、肝胃热盛证、瘀滞胃肠证、热毒蕴肠证、肠道瘀滞证，或内痔、肛裂、锁肛痔、肠癌、胃癌、小肠瘅、臌胀等。又称大便带血。便血量多见于肠风络伤证，或痔疮、肛裂、胃瘅、小肠瘅、肠结等。便血少见于肝肾阴虚证、脾肾阳虚证，或肠癌、肠瘤、肠痨、胃癌等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Blood preceding the stool, blood following the stool, blood mixed with the stool, or blood alone passed from the bowel. Seen in intestinal wind damaging the collaterals pattern, intestinal dampness-heat pattern, liver-kidney yin deficiency pattern, spleen-kidney yang deficiency pattern, spleen deficiency with qi sinking pattern, blood heat stirring the blood pattern, liver-stomach heat exuberance pattern, stasis in the stomach and intestines pattern, heat-toxin accumulating in the intestines pattern, and intestinal stasis pattern, or internal hemorrhoids, anal fissure, anorectal cancer, intestinal cancer, stomach cancer, small-intestine dan, and tympanites. Also known as blood in the stool. Profuse bloody stool is mostly seen in intestinal wind damaging the collaterals pattern, or hemorrhoids, anal fissure, stomach dan, small-intestine dan, and intestinal binding; scanty bloody stool is seen in liver-kidney yin deficiency pattern and spleen-kidney yang deficiency pattern, or intestinal cancer, intestinal tumor, intestinal consumption, and stomach cancer.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.4.1.43</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:synonym>便下脓血</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:synonym>大便带血便血量多</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:synonym>大便潜血阳性</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0002573</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:severityText>重度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>持续性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>受凉、劳累</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>药物治疗</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:snomedCT>405737000</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>Hematochezia</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:icd11>ME24.A</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Digestive tract haemorrhage</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_便血</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Blood preceding the stool, blood following the stool, blood mixed with the stool, or blood alone passed from the bowel. Seen in intestinal wind damaging the collaterals pattern, intestinal dampness-heat pattern, liver-kidney yin deficiency pattern, spleen-kidney yang deficiency pattern, spleen deficiency with qi sinking pattern, blood heat stirring the blood pattern, liver-stomach heat exuberance pattern, stasis in the stomach and intestines pattern, heat-toxin accumulating in the intestines pattern, and intestinal stasis pattern, or internal hemorrhoids, anal fissure, anorectal cancer, intestinal cancer, stomach cancer, small-intestine dan, and tympanites. Also known as blood in the stool. Profuse bloody stool is mostly seen in intestinal wind damaging the collaterals pattern, or hemorrhoids, anal fissure, stomach dan, small-intestine dan, and intestinal binding; scanty bloody stool is seen in liver-kidney yin deficiency pattern and spleen-kidney yang deficiency pattern, or intestinal cancer, intestinal tumor, intestinal consumption, and stomach cancer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>便下脓血</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
