        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/f#ClinicalFinding"/>
      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">鼻中因痒而气喷作于声，由于人体阳气振作以抗邪的一种表现。如喷嚏频作，并伴有其它不适症状，则为病态。见于风寒袭鼻证、肺虚鼻窍失煦证、脾虚鼻窍失照、阳虚鼻窍失煦证、郁热熏鼻证，或伤风鼻塞、感冒、麻疹初期、鼻鼽等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Noisy expulsion of air from the nose due to itching—a manifestation of the body's yang qi rising to resist the pathogen; frequent sneezing with other discomforts is pathological. Seen in wind-cold attacking the nose pattern, lung deficiency with the nasal orifices unwarmed pattern, spleen deficiency with the nasal orifices unilluminated pattern, yang deficiency with the nasal orifices unwarmed pattern, and depressed heat fumigating the nose pattern, or wind-damage nasal obstruction, common cold, early measles, and allergic rhinitis (biqiu).</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.6.2.17</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0025095</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>每日多次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>饮食不当</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>药物治疗</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:snomedCT>76067001</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>Sneezing</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:icd11>MD11.9</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Sneezing</tcm:icd11Term>
  
