      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">视物旋转动荡，或眼前有蚊蝇飞动之感。见于风热犯目证、水轮湿热证、肉轮风痰阻络证、肝郁气滞证、心神不宁证、气血两虚证、肝肾亏虚证、脾气虚弱证、命门火衰证，或圆翳内障、胎患内障、黄心内障、五风内障、偃月侵睛、花翳白陷、凝脂翳、黄液上冲、旋螺尖起、黑翳如珠、瞳睛病、正漏、混睛障、赤膜下垂、血翳包睛、宿翳、飞蚊幻视症、远视、近视、视瞻昏渺、高风内障、血灌瞳神、物损真睛、眯目飞扬、椒疮、倒睫拳毛、暴风客热、天行赤眼、金疳、火疳、白膜侵睛、赤丝虬脉、赤脉传睛、胬肉攀睛等。又称目眩。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Objects appearing to rotate and sway, or a sensation of mosquitoes and flies moving before the eyes. Seen in wind-heat invading the eye pattern, water-wheel dampness-heat pattern, flesh-wheel wind-phlegm blocking the collaterals pattern, liver depression with qi stagnation pattern, heart-spirit restlessness pattern, qi-blood dual deficiency pattern, liver-kidney deficiency pattern, spleen qi weakness pattern, and mingmen fire decline pattern, or round-nebula internal obstruction (cataract), fetal internal obstruction, yellow-center internal obstruction, five-wind internal obstruction, crescent-moon invading the eye, flower-nebula white sinking, congealed-fat nebula, yellow fluid surging upward (hypopyon), spiral-cone protrusion, black nebula like a pearl, pupil disease, mixed-eye impediment, red membrane hanging down, blood nebula enveloping the eye, old nebula, floaters (muscae volitantes), hyperopia, myopia, dim and hazy vision, high-wind internal obstruction (retinitis pigmentosa), blood flooding the pupil (hyphema), traumatic eye injury, trachoma (pepper sores), trichiasis, storm-like invading heat (acute conjunctivitis), epidemic red eye, golden gan (phlyctenular conjunctivitis), fire gan (scleritis), white membrane invading the eye, red tortuous vessels, red vessels spreading onto the eye, and pterygium. Also known as dazzling (muyun).</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.6.1.11</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:synonym>目眩</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:severityText>中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>数小时一次</tcm:frequencyText>
