    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>blurred vision</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:snomedCT>246636008</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>blurred vision</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_眼花</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Objects appearing to rotate and sway, or a sensation of mosquitoes and flies moving before the eyes. Seen in wind-heat invading the eye pattern, water-wheel dampness-heat pattern, flesh-wheel wind-phlegm blocking the collaterals pattern, liver depression with qi stagnation pattern, heart-spirit restlessness pattern, qi-blood dual deficiency pattern, liver-kidney deficiency pattern, spleen qi weakness pattern, and mingmen fire decline pattern, or round-nebula internal obstruction (cataract), fetal internal obstruction, yellow-center internal obstruction, five-wind internal obstruction, crescent-moon invading the eye, flower-nebula white sinking, congealed-fat nebula, yellow fluid surging upward (hypopyon), spiral-cone protrusion, black nebula like a pearl, pupil disease, mixed-eye impediment, red membrane hanging down, blood nebula enveloping the eye, old nebula, floaters (muscae volitantes), hyperopia, myopia, dim and hazy vision, high-wind internal obstruction (retinitis pigmentosa), blood flooding the pupil (hyphema), traumatic eye injury, trachoma (pepper sores), trichiasis, storm-like invading heat (acute conjunctivitis), epidemic red eye, golden gan (phlyctenular conjunctivitis), fire gan (scleritis), white membrane invading the eye, red tortuous vessels, red vessels spreading onto the eye, and pterygium. Also known as dazzling (muyun).</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>目眩</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
