        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/e#RestRel"/>
      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
      <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="N78bd9c7d13c4455bbb1ede9e848c53fb">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/accompanies"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/f#ClinicalFinding"/>
      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">脉来缓慢，一息三到四至（1分钟不满60次）。见于胃阳虚证，或胸阳不畅、结胸、癥瘕、沉寒痼冷、热入血室等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">The pulse coming slowly, three to four beats per breath (fewer than 60 beats per minute). Seen in stomach yang deficiency pattern, or chest yang obstruction, chest binding (jiexiong), abdominal masses (zhengjia), deep-seated stubborn cold, and heat entering the blood chamber.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.2.2.32</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>中度至重度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>偶尔发作</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>受凉、劳累</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>休息、保暖</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_脉迟</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>The pulse coming slowly, three to four beats per breath (fewer than 60 beats per minute). Seen in stomach yang deficiency pattern, or chest yang obstruction, chest binding (jiexiong), abdominal masses (zhengjia), deep-seated stubborn cold, and heat entering the blood chamber.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
      <owl:Restriction>
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/dueTo"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/e#FireEvil"/>
      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
  </owl:Class>
