      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">发作性的精神恍惚，甚则突然仆倒，昏不知人，口吐白沫，两目上视，四肢抽搐，口中作猪羊叫声，移时苏醒。见于痫病风痰闭神证、痰热内扰证、脾虚痰湿证、痰阻清窍证、肝郁痰火证、肝肾阴虚证、血虚动风证等。又称羊癫风、羊痫风等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Paroxysmal mental trance, or even sudden collapse with unconsciousness, foaming at the mouth, upward turning of the eyes, convulsions of the limbs, and pig- or goat-like cries, regaining consciousness after a while. Seen in xian (epilepsy) with wind-phlegm blocking the spirit pattern, phlegm-heat internal disturbance pattern, spleen deficiency with phlegm-dampness pattern, phlegm blocking the clear orifices pattern, liver depression with phlegm-fire pattern, liver-kidney yin deficiency pattern, and blood deficiency stirring wind pattern. Also known as goat-convulsion wind (yangdianfeng).</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.4.1.3</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:synonym>羊痫风</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:synonym>羊癫风</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度至中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>偶尔发作</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>环境刺激</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>药物治疗</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0033052</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0011146</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:snomedCT>246545002</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>epilepsy</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_痫</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Paroxysmal mental trance, or even sudden collapse with unconsciousness, foaming at the mouth, upward turning of the eyes, convulsions of the limbs, and pig- or goat-like cries, regaining consciousness after a while. Seen in xian (epilepsy) with wind-phlegm blocking the spirit pattern, phlegm-heat internal disturbance pattern, spleen deficiency with phlegm-dampness pattern, phlegm blocking the clear orifices pattern, liver depression with phlegm-fire pattern, liver-kidney yin deficiency pattern, and blood deficiency stirring wind pattern. Also known as goat-convulsion wind (yangdianfeng).</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>羊痫风</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>羊癫风</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
