      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">自觉咽喉部似有物梗阻不适，咯之不出，咽之不下，但并不妨碍进食。见于心脾两虚证、肝气郁结证、肝郁脾虚证、肝胃不和证、阴虚肝郁证，或梅核气、慢喉痹、茎突综合征、咽喉肿瘤、食管瘅、胃病、血劳等。又称喉中梗阻感。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">A subjective sensation of something stuck in the throat—unable to be coughed up or swallowed down—without interfering with eating. Seen in heart-spleen dual deficiency pattern, liver qi depression pattern, liver depression with spleen deficiency pattern, liver-stomach disharmony pattern, and yin deficiency with liver depression pattern, or plum-pit qi (globus pharyngis), chronic throat bi (pharyngitis), styloid process syndrome, throat tumor, esophageal dan, stomach disease, and blood consumption. Also known as obstructive sensation in the throat.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.6.2.8</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>偶尔发作</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>饮食不当</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>药物治疗</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_咽部堵塞感</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A subjective sensation of something stuck in the throat—unable to be coughed up or swallowed down—without interfering with eating. Seen in heart-spleen dual deficiency pattern, liver qi depression pattern, liver depression with spleen deficiency pattern, liver-stomach disharmony pattern, and yin deficiency with liver depression pattern, or plum-pit qi (globus pharyngis), chronic throat bi (pharyngitis), styloid process syndrome, throat tumor, esophageal dan, stomach disease, and blood consumption. Also known as obstructive sensation in the throat.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
      <owl:Restriction>
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/dueTo"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/e#EmotionE"/>
      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
  </owl:Class>
