    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">小儿头颅较正常小。见于先天不足、风湿痰热毒邪侵袭、肝肾亏虚证，或尖颅等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">The head smaller than normal in children. Seen in congenital insufficiency, invasion by wind-dampness-phlegm-heat-toxin pathogens, and liver-kidney deficiency pattern, or oxycephaly (tower skull).</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.6.8.1.11</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度至中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>偶尔发作</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>感染、过敏</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>休息、保暖</tcm:reliefText>
