    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">脉来浮取弦急搏指，按之空虚，中空外坚。见于气虚不固、血虚证、虚劳疾病、亡血、精血亏虚证，或失精、漏下等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">A pulse that on light pressure feels wiry, urgent and bounding to the finger, but on heavy pressure feels empty—hollow inside and firm outside (leather/drumskin pulse). Seen in qi deficiency insecurity, blood deficiency pattern, deficiency-consumption diseases, blood collapse, and essence-blood deficiency pattern, or seminal loss and leaking (louxia).</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.2.2.42</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>偶尔发作</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>情绪波动</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>情绪调节</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_脉革</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A pulse that on light pressure feels wiry, urgent and bounding to the finger, but on heavy pressure feels empty—hollow inside and firm outside (leather/drumskin pulse). Seen in qi deficiency insecurity, blood deficiency pattern, deficiency-consumption diseases, blood collapse, and essence-blood deficiency pattern, or seminal loss and leaking (louxia).</obo:IAO_0000115>
