    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/f#PsychiatricFinding"/>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">心跳快或节律不齐，或自觉心中悸动不宁。见于心气虚证、心阳虚证、心阴虚证、心血虚证、痰热扰心证、水气凌心证、心脾气血两虚证、阴虚火旺证、心虚神怯证、瘀阻心脉证，或心痹、心瘅、胸痹、肺心病、心衰、风眩、厥心痛、高原胸痹、心郁、支饮、梅毒攻心、脚气冲心、神劳、神郁、中恶、风厥、瘿劳、黑疸、虚劳类疾病、饥厥、血脱、液脱、蚕豆黄等。又称心跳、心动悸。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Rapid or irregular heartbeat, or a subjective sensation of fluttering unease in the heart. Seen in heart qi deficiency pattern, heart yang deficiency pattern, heart yin deficiency pattern, heart blood deficiency pattern, phlegm-heat disturbing the heart pattern, water-qi intimidating the heart pattern, heart-spleen qi-blood dual deficiency pattern, yin deficiency with fire flaring pattern, heart deficiency with timid spirit pattern, and stasis obstructing the heart vessels pattern, or heart bi, heart dan, chest bi (angina), pulmonary heart disease, heart failure, wind dizziness (fengxuan), reversal heart pain, high-altitude chest bi, heart depression, propping rheum (zhiyin), syphilis attacking the heart, beriberi rushing to the heart, spirit overstrain, spirit depression, zhong'e (sudden turmoil), wind reversal, goiter consumption, black jaundice, deficiency-consumption diseases, hunger reversal, blood collapse, humor collapse, and favism (candouhuang). Also known as heartbeat awareness and stirring palpitation.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.5.2.62</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:synonym>心跳</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:synonym>心动悸</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0001962</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:snomedCT>80313002</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>Palpitations</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:icd11>MC81.3</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Palpitations</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_心悸</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Rapid or irregular heartbeat, or a subjective sensation of fluttering unease in the heart. Seen in heart qi deficiency pattern, heart yang deficiency pattern, heart yin deficiency pattern, heart blood deficiency pattern, phlegm-heat disturbing the heart pattern, water-qi intimidating the heart pattern, heart-spleen qi-blood dual deficiency pattern, yin deficiency with fire flaring pattern, heart deficiency with timid spirit pattern, and stasis obstructing the heart vessels pattern, or heart bi, heart dan, chest bi (angina), pulmonary heart disease, heart failure, wind dizziness (fengxuan), reversal heart pain, high-altitude chest bi, heart depression, propping rheum (zhiyin), syphilis attacking the heart, beriberi rushing to the heart, spirit overstrain, spirit depression, zhong'e (sudden turmoil), wind reversal, goiter consumption, black jaundice, deficiency-consumption diseases, hunger reversal, blood collapse, humor collapse, and favism (candouhuang). Also known as heartbeat awareness and stirring palpitation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>心跳</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>心动悸</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>HPO:HP:0001962</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0001962"/>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:80313002</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://snomed.info/id/80313002"/>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ICD11:MC81.3</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
  
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
