    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/f#cat_睡眠类"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/f#PsychiatricFinding"/>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">并不因惊吓，而自觉心悸不安，不能自制，多伴心跳节律不齐，全身情况较差，病情较重。见于心气虚证、心阳虚证、心阴虚证、心血虚证、痰热扰心证、水气凌心证、心脾气血两虚证、阴虚火旺证、心虚神怯证、瘀阻心脉证，或心痹、心瘅、胸痹、肺心病、心衰、风眩、厥心痛、高原胸痹、支饮、梅毒攻心、脚气冲心、风厥、瘿劳、黑疸、饥厥、血脱、液脱、蚕豆黄等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Palpitations and unease occurring without fright, beyond self-control, usually accompanied by irregular heart rhythm, poor general condition and severe disease. Seen in heart qi deficiency pattern, heart yang deficiency pattern, heart yin deficiency pattern, heart blood deficiency pattern, phlegm-heat disturbing the heart pattern, water-qi intimidating the heart pattern, heart-spleen qi-blood dual deficiency pattern, yin deficiency with fire flaring pattern, heart deficiency with timid spirit pattern, and stasis obstructing the heart vessels pattern, or heart bi, heart dan, chest bi, pulmonary heart disease, heart failure, wind dizziness, reversal heart pain, high-altitude chest bi, propping rheum, syphilis attacking the heart, beriberi rushing to the heart, wind reversal, goiter consumption, black jaundice, hunger reversal, blood collapse, humor collapse, and favism.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.5.2.49</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>重度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>数小时一次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>环境刺激</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>饮食调整</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0001962</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:snomedCT>80313002</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>Palpitations</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:icd11>MC81.3</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Palpitations</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_怔忡</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Palpitations and unease occurring without fright, beyond self-control, usually accompanied by irregular heart rhythm, poor general condition and severe disease. Seen in heart qi deficiency pattern, heart yang deficiency pattern, heart yin deficiency pattern, heart blood deficiency pattern, phlegm-heat disturbing the heart pattern, water-qi intimidating the heart pattern, heart-spleen qi-blood dual deficiency pattern, yin deficiency with fire flaring pattern, heart deficiency with timid spirit pattern, and stasis obstructing the heart vessels pattern, or heart bi, heart dan, chest bi, pulmonary heart disease, heart failure, wind dizziness, reversal heart pain, high-altitude chest bi, propping rheum, syphilis attacking the heart, beriberi rushing to the heart, wind reversal, goiter consumption, black jaundice, hunger reversal, blood collapse, humor collapse, and favism.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>HPO:HP:0001962</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
