    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Clouded consciousness, even coma—unresponsive to calling. Seen in heat blocking the heart-spirit pattern, phlegm-heat disturbing the spirit pattern, phlegm clouding the heart-spirit pattern, stasis obstructing the brain collaterals pattern, summerheat blocking the pericardium pattern, dryness-heat internal binding pattern, turbid toxin blocking the spirit pattern, liver yang transforming into wind pattern, and internal blockage with external collapse pattern, or head internal injury, summerheat reversal, cold reversal, hunger reversal, food or drug poisoning, wind reversal, coal-gas poisoning, hanging, drowning, electric injury, qi reversal, blood reversal, phlegm reversal, zhong'e, pneumonia with panting cough, pestilential-toxic dysentery, summerheat-warmth, spring-warmth, bleeding wind stroke, ischemic wind stroke, reversal heart pain, heat entering the blood chamber, eclampsia (zixian), blood collapse, humor collapse, ding sores running yellow (septicemia), ju-toxin sinking inward, postpartum convulsive disease, neonatal tetanus, infantile acute and chronic fright wind, kidney reversal, liver reversal, wasting-thirst reversal, lung reversal, corpse reversal, and goiter consumption. Also known as coma and stupor.</obo:IAO_0000115>
