      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">脉动势弱力薄，举之无力，按之空豁，应指松软。是一切无力脉的总称。见于气血两虚证、气虚证，或肺痿、伤暑、多汗、惊悸等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">A pulse weak in force—powerless on lifting, empty on pressing, and soft under the finger; the collective term for all forceless pulses. Seen in qi-blood dual deficiency pattern and qi deficiency pattern, or lung wilt (feiwei), summerheat injury, profuse sweating, and fearful palpitations.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.2.2.11</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>每日多次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>感染、过敏</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>药物治疗</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_脉虚</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A pulse weak in force—powerless on lifting, empty on pressing, and soft under the finger; the collective term for all forceless pulses. Seen in qi-blood dual deficiency pattern and qi deficiency pattern, or lung wilt (feiwei), summerheat injury, profuse sweating, and fearful palpitations.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  
