    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">婴幼儿的头形超出该发育阶段头形的正常范围。见于先天不足、风湿痰热毒邪侵袭、肝肾亏虚证，或解颅等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">An infant's or toddler's head size exceeds the normal range for the developmental stage. Seen in congenital insufficiency, invasion by wind-damp-phlegm-heat toxin, liver-kidney deficiency pattern, or cranial fissure non-closure (jielu/hydrocephalus).</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.6.8.1.31</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>间歇性</tcm:frequencyText>
