    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">颈部细于正常人。见于气血两虚证、阴虚证，或癥瘕、噎膈等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">The neck is thinner than that of a normal person. Seen in dual deficiency of qi and blood pattern, yin deficiency pattern, or abdominal masses (zhengjia) and dysphagia-occlusion (yege).</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.6.3.11</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>重度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>数小时一次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>情绪波动</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>饮食调整</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0035007</tcm:hpoID>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_颈细</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>The neck is thinner than that of a normal person. Seen in dual deficiency of qi and blood pattern, yin deficiency pattern, or abdominal masses (zhengjia) and dysphagia-occlusion (yege).</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>HPO:HP:0035007</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    <skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0035007"/>
