    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">耳中如有鸣响，或大或小或高或低。见于风热袭肺证、肝火亢盛证、肝阳上亢证、肝血虚证、肾阴虚证、肾气不足证、心肾不交证、脾胃气虚证、气滞血瘀证等。突起耳鸣见于血瘀耳窍证、痰火闭耳证、肝火燔耳证，或气厥、风眩、耵耳、异物人耳、暴聋耳鸣、脑瘤、耳眩晕等。经常耳鸣见于肝肾阴虚证、肾气虚证、肾精亏虚证、气虚耳窍失充证、血虚耳窍失养证、血瘀耳窍证，或耳闭等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Perception of ringing sounds in the ear(s), varying in loudness and pitch. Seen in wind-heat invading the lung pattern, hyperactive liver fire pattern, liver yang hyperactivity pattern, liver blood deficiency pattern, kidney yin deficiency pattern, kidney qi insufficiency pattern, heart-kidney non-interaction pattern, spleen-stomach qi deficiency pattern, or qi stagnation with blood stasis pattern. Sudden-onset tinnitus is seen in blood stasis in the ear orifice pattern, phlegm-fire blocking the ear pattern, liver fire flaring the ear pattern, or qi syncope, wind dizziness, cerumen obstruction, foreign body in the ear, sudden deafness with tinnitus, brain tumor, or ear vertigo. Recurrent/chronic tinnitus is seen in liver-kidney yin deficiency pattern, kidney qi deficiency pattern, kidney essence deficiency pattern, qi deficiency with underfilled ear orifice pattern, blood deficiency with unnourished ear orifice pattern, blood stasis in the ear orifice pattern, or ear blockage (erbi).</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.6.2.34</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0000360</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:snomedCT>60862001</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>Tinnitus</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:icd11>MC41</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Tinnitus</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_耳鸣</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Perception of ringing sounds in the ear(s), varying in loudness and pitch. Seen in wind-heat invading the lung pattern, hyperactive liver fire pattern, liver yang hyperactivity pattern, liver blood deficiency pattern, kidney yin deficiency pattern, kidney qi insufficiency pattern, heart-kidney non-interaction pattern, spleen-stomach qi deficiency pattern, or qi stagnation with blood stasis pattern. Sudden-onset tinnitus is seen in blood stasis in the ear orifice pattern, phlegm-fire blocking the ear pattern, liver fire flaring the ear pattern, or qi syncope, wind dizziness, cerumen obstruction, foreign body in the ear, sudden deafness with tinnitus, brain tumor, or ear vertigo. Recurrent/chronic tinnitus is seen in liver-kidney yin deficiency pattern, kidney qi deficiency pattern, kidney essence deficiency pattern, qi deficiency with underfilled ear orifice pattern, blood deficiency with unnourished ear orifice pattern, blood stasis in the ear orifice pattern, or ear blockage (erbi).</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>HPO:HP:0000360</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0000360"/>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:60862001</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://snomed.info/id/60862001"/>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ICD11:MC41</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
  
