    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">人夜啼哭不安，或每夜定时啼哭，甚则通宵达旦，但白天如常，或伴神疲、困倦。见于脾阳虚证，或婴儿昼夜节律未调（婴儿夜啼证），或小儿疳积、受惊吓等。又称小儿夜啼。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">An infant cries restlessly at night, sometimes at a fixed time each night or even throughout the night, while behaving normally during the day, possibly accompanied by listlessness and drowsiness. Seen in spleen yang deficiency pattern, immature day-night rhythm in infants (infantile night crying), or infantile malnutrition with accumulation (ganji) and fright. Also known as infantile night crying.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.4.1.40</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:synonym>小儿夜啼</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:severityText>中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>偶尔发作</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>环境刺激</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>情绪调节</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:icd11>SE36</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Night crying disorder (TM1)</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_夜啼</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>An infant cries restlessly at night, sometimes at a fixed time each night or even throughout the night, while behaving normally during the day, possibly accompanied by listlessness and drowsiness. Seen in spleen yang deficiency pattern, immature day-night rhythm in infants (infantile night crying), or infantile malnutrition with accumulation (ganji) and fright. Also known as infantile night crying.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>小儿夜啼</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ICD11:SE36</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
  
