    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">脉体短缩，不能满部，不及正常脉象之长，应指于寸、关部或寸部、尺部沉弱，唯关部明显。见于气虚证、痰气、食积、气逆等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">A pulse whose length is shortened and does not fill its normal position(s); it may respond weakly at the cun and chi positions with only the guan position palpable. Seen in qi deficiency pattern, phlegm-qi disorders, food accumulation, or qi counterflow.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.2.2.45</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>数小时一次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>受凉、劳累</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>情绪调节</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_脉短</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A pulse whose length is shortened and does not fill its normal position(s); it may respond weakly at the cun and chi positions with only the guan position palpable. Seen in qi deficiency pattern, phlegm-qi disorders, food accumulation, or qi counterflow.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  
