    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">恶寒与发热交替发作，先有恶寒，甚或寒战，随即发热，但在傍晚后加重或明显。见于伤寒邪入少阳、疟疾寒证。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Alternating chills and fever—first aversion to cold or even rigor, then fever—that worsens or becomes pronounced after dusk. Seen in cold damage with the pathogen entering the shaoyang stage, or cold-type malaria.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.1.3.5</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>重度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>数小时一次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>自身免疫反应</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>退热药物、休息</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:icd11>SD93</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Alternating fever and chills disorder (TM1)</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_寒热往来_入暮尤剧</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Alternating chills and fever—first aversion to cold or even rigor, then fever—that worsens or becomes pronounced after dusk. Seen in cold damage with the pathogen entering the shaoyang stage, or cold-type malaria.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ICD11:SD93</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
  
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
