    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">自觉心无所托，恍恍然跳动不安。见于心气虚证、心阳虚证、心阴虚证、心血虚证、痰热扰心证、水气凌心证、心脾气血两虚证、阴虚火旺证、心虚神怯证、瘀阻心脉证，或心痹、心瘅、胸痹、肺心病、心衰、风眩、厥心痛、高原胸痹、心郁、支饮、梅毒攻心、脚气冲心、神劳、神郁、中恶、风厥、瘿劳、黑疸、虚劳类疾病、饥厥、血脱、液脱、蚕豆黄等。多为快速心律失常。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">A feeling of the heart being unsupported and beating restlessly with vague unease. Seen in heart qi deficiency pattern, heart yang deficiency pattern, heart yin deficiency pattern, heart blood deficiency pattern, phlegm-heat harassing the heart pattern, water qi intimidating the heart pattern, heart-spleen qi-blood dual deficiency pattern, yin deficiency with effulgent fire pattern, heart deficiency with timid spirit pattern, stasis obstructing the heart vessels pattern, or heart impediment, heart heat (xindan), chest impediment, pulmonary heart disease, heart failure, wind dizziness (hypertension), jue heart pain, high-altitude chest impediment, heart depression, propping rheum (zhiyin), syphilis attacking the heart, beriberi rushing to the heart, spirit taxation, spirit depression, malignity attack (zhonge), wind syncope, goiter taxation, black jaundice, deficiency-taxation diseases, hunger syncope, blood collapse, fluid collapse, or favism (candouhuang). Mostly corresponds to tachyarrhythmia.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.5.2.44</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>重度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>偶尔发作</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>感染、过敏</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>饮食调整</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0001676</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:snomedCT>80313002</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>heart palpitations</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:icd11>MC81.2</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Palpitations</tcm:icd11Term>
  
