    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A feeling of the heart being unsupported and beating restlessly with vague unease. Seen in heart qi deficiency pattern, heart yang deficiency pattern, heart yin deficiency pattern, heart blood deficiency pattern, phlegm-heat harassing the heart pattern, water qi intimidating the heart pattern, heart-spleen qi-blood dual deficiency pattern, yin deficiency with effulgent fire pattern, heart deficiency with timid spirit pattern, stasis obstructing the heart vessels pattern, or heart impediment, heart heat (xindan), chest impediment, pulmonary heart disease, heart failure, wind dizziness (hypertension), jue heart pain, high-altitude chest impediment, heart depression, propping rheum (zhiyin), syphilis attacking the heart, beriberi rushing to the heart, spirit taxation, spirit depression, malignity attack (zhonge), wind syncope, goiter taxation, black jaundice, deficiency-taxation diseases, hunger syncope, blood collapse, fluid collapse, or favism (candouhuang). Mostly corresponds to tachyarrhythmia.</obo:IAO_0000115>
