    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">脉体阔大倍于常，但无汹涌之势。见于阳热邪盛有余、亡血证，或虚劳病等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">A pulse body broad and large, about double the normal, but without a surging force. Seen in exuberant yang-heat pathogen, blood collapse pattern, or deficiency-taxation diseases.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.2.2.34</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>持续性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>感染、过敏</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>饮食调整</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_脉大</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A pulse body broad and large, about double the normal, but without a surging force. Seen in exuberant yang-heat pathogen, blood collapse pattern, or deficiency-taxation diseases.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  
