    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">脉来形细，搏动往来迟滞坚涩，不流利，应如轻刀刮竹。见于伤精，血少、血瘀证，或血痹、脱液、失血、虚劳、积聚等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">A thin, rough pulse that comes and goes sluggishly, unsmooth, feeling like scraping bamboo with a light knife. Seen in essence damage, blood deficiency, blood stasis pattern, or blood impediment, fluid collapse, blood loss, deficiency-taxation, or accumulation-gathering (jiju).</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.2.2.6</tcm:reference>
