    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">心中急躁，冲动不安。见于阴虚阳亢证、痰气郁结证，或风眩、神劳、癫病、狂病、瘿气等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Inner irritability and impulsiveness with restlessness. Seen in yin deficiency with yang hyperactivity pattern, phlegm-qi stagnation pattern, or wind dizziness (hypertension), spirit taxation, depressive psychosis (dian), manic psychosis (kuang), or goiter qi disorder.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.4.1.34</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:synonym>急躁</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:severityText>重度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>间歇性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>情绪波动</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>休息、保暖</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_性急</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Inner irritability and impulsiveness with restlessness. Seen in yin deficiency with yang hyperactivity pattern, phlegm-qi stagnation pattern, or wind dizziness (hypertension), spirit taxation, depressive psychosis (dian), manic psychosis (kuang), or goiter qi disorder.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>急躁</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
  
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
      <owl:Restriction>
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/dueTo"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/e#PhlegmEvil"/>
      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
