    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">脉来极细极软，按之欲绝，似有若无，体象模糊，浮候沉候无明显区别。见于气血两虚证、气虚证、血虚证、阳虚证、阴阳两虚证或之阳等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">An extremely thin and faint pulse that seems about to expire on pressure, as if present yet absent, with indistinct contour and little difference between superficial and deep palpation. Seen in dual deficiency of qi and blood pattern, qi deficiency pattern, blood deficiency pattern, yang deficiency pattern, or yin-yang dual deficiency pattern.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.2.2.12</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度至中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>偶尔发作</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>饮食不当</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>情绪调节</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_脉微</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>An extremely thin and faint pulse that seems about to expire on pressure, as if present yet absent, with indistinct contour and little difference between superficial and deep palpation. Seen in dual deficiency of qi and blood pattern, qi deficiency pattern, blood deficiency pattern, yang deficiency pattern, or yin-yang dual deficiency pattern.</obo:IAO_0000115>
