    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">黑睛渍破，黄仁自溃口绽出。见于阴虚火旺证、肝胆火炽证、风轮湿热证、风轮热毒证、风轮阴虚证等。又称损翳。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">The cornea ulcerates and ruptures, with the iris prolapsing through the opening (iris prolapse). Seen in yin deficiency with effulgent fire pattern, liver-gallbladder blazing fire pattern, wind-wheel (cornea) dampness-heat pattern, wind-wheel heat toxin pattern, or wind-wheel yin deficiency pattern. Also known as damaged nebula (sunyi).</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.6.10.1.104</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:synonym>损翳</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:severityText>重度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>数小时一次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>饮食不当</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>情绪调节</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_目如蟹睛</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>The cornea ulcerates and ruptures, with the iris prolapsing through the opening (iris prolapse). Seen in yin deficiency with effulgent fire pattern, liver-gallbladder blazing fire pattern, wind-wheel (cornea) dampness-heat pattern, wind-wheel heat toxin pattern, or wind-wheel yin deficiency pattern. Also known as damaged nebula (sunyi).</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>损翳</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
  
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
      <owl:Restriction>
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/dueTo"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/e#DampnessEvil"/>
      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
