      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">脉来形直体长，搏动稳重且弛张度较大。见于肝气郁结证、肝阳上亢证、气滞证，或痉病、痫、水气、疟疾、痉腹病等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">A pulse that is straight and long in shape, with a steady beat and marked tensile resilience (like a bowstring). Seen in liver qi depression pattern, liver yang hyperactivity pattern, qi stagnation pattern, or convulsive disease, epilepsy (xian), water qi disorder, malaria, or spastic abdominal disease.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.2.2.26</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度至中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>每日多次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>情绪波动</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>情绪调节</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_脉弦</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A pulse that is straight and long in shape, with a steady beat and marked tensile resilience (like a bowstring). Seen in liver qi depression pattern, liver yang hyperactivity pattern, qi stagnation pattern, or convulsive disease, epilepsy (xian), water qi disorder, malaria, or spastic abdominal disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  </owl:Class>
