    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/f#cat_睡眠类"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/f#PsychiatricFinding"/>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">欲吐不吐，欲罢不止。见于寒邪犯胃证、食滞胃肠证、胃热炽盛证、寒饮停胃证、肝胃不和证、脾胃气虚证、脾胃阳虚证、胃阴虚证、湿热蕴脾证、暑湿内蕴证、虫扰胆膈证，或妊娠恶阻、胆瘅、肝瘟、胃反、食管瘅、胃郁、食物中毒、类霍乱、伤食等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Feeling like vomiting without vomiting, unable to stop the urge. Seen in cold pathogen invading the stomach pattern, food stagnating in the stomach and intestines pattern, stomach fire blazing pattern, cold rheum collecting in the stomach pattern, liver-stomach disharmony pattern, spleen-stomach qi deficiency pattern, spleen-stomach yang deficiency pattern, stomach yin deficiency pattern, dampness-heat accumulating in the spleen pattern, summerheat-dampness internal accumulation pattern, worm disturbing the gallbladder-diaphragm pattern, or morning sickness of pregnancy (pernicious vomiting), gallbladder heat (dan dan), liver pestilence (severe hepatitis), stomach reflux, esophageal inflammation, stomach depression, food poisoning, cholera-like disease, or food damage.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.3.10</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:synonym>恶心欲呕</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0002018</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:snomedCT>422587007</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>Nausea</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:icd11>MD90</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Nausea or vomiting</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_恶心</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Feeling like vomiting without vomiting, unable to stop the urge. Seen in cold pathogen invading the stomach pattern, food stagnating in the stomach and intestines pattern, stomach fire blazing pattern, cold rheum collecting in the stomach pattern, liver-stomach disharmony pattern, spleen-stomach qi deficiency pattern, spleen-stomach yang deficiency pattern, stomach yin deficiency pattern, dampness-heat accumulating in the spleen pattern, summerheat-dampness internal accumulation pattern, worm disturbing the gallbladder-diaphragm pattern, or morning sickness of pregnancy (pernicious vomiting), gallbladder heat (dan dan), liver pestilence (severe hepatitis), stomach reflux, esophageal inflammation, stomach depression, food poisoning, cholera-like disease, or food damage.</obo:IAO_0000115>
