    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">精神倦怠，自觉疲乏无力。见于气血两虚证、湿困脾胃证、痰湿内蕴证、暑伤气阴证、暑湿证、肝胆湿热证、脾肾阳虚证、脾虚湿困证、心脾气虚证、肝肾阴虚证，或神劳、血劳、瘿劳、肌痿、肝著、心衰、伤暑、㾏夏、肥胖病等。又称少神。可与困倦同见，又称神困、神倦。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Listlessness with subjective tiredness and lack of strength. Seen in dual deficiency of qi and blood pattern, dampness encumbering the spleen-stomach pattern, phlegm-dampness internal accumulation pattern, summerheat damaging qi and yin pattern, summerheat-dampness pattern, liver-gallbladder dampness-heat pattern, spleen-kidney yang deficiency pattern, spleen deficiency with dampness encumbrance pattern, heart-spleen qi deficiency pattern, liver-kidney yin deficiency pattern, or spirit taxation, blood taxation, goiter taxation, muscle atrophy, liver fixity, heart failure, summerheat injury, summer fever of children, or obesity. Also known as scant spirit; when occurring together with drowsiness it is called spirit tiredness or spirit weariness.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.4.1.9</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:synonym>少神可与困倦同</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>偶尔发作</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>受凉、劳累</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>情绪调节</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0033630</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0033236</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:icd11>MG22</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Fatigue</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_神疲</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Listlessness with subjective tiredness and lack of strength. Seen in dual deficiency of qi and blood pattern, dampness encumbering the spleen-stomach pattern, phlegm-dampness internal accumulation pattern, summerheat damaging qi and yin pattern, summerheat-dampness pattern, liver-gallbladder dampness-heat pattern, spleen-kidney yang deficiency pattern, spleen deficiency with dampness encumbrance pattern, heart-spleen qi deficiency pattern, liver-kidney yin deficiency pattern, or spirit taxation, blood taxation, goiter taxation, muscle atrophy, liver fixity, heart failure, summerheat injury, summer fever of children, or obesity. Also known as scant spirit; when occurring together with drowsiness it is called spirit tiredness or spirit weariness.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>少神可与困倦同</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>HPO:HP:0033630</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
