    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">无故悲伤，或感到悲痛，或常欲哭，不能自制。见于心脾气结证、肺气虚证，或脏躁、中风等。又称喜悲伤欲哭。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Groundless sadness, feelings of grief, or a frequent urge to weep that cannot be controlled. Seen in heart-spleen qi binding pattern, lung qi deficiency pattern, or visceral agitation (zangzao) and stroke. Also known as proneness to grief with desire to weep.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.4.1.13</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:synonym>喜悲伤欲哭</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度至中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>偶尔发作</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>环境刺激</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>情绪调节</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_善悲</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Groundless sadness, feelings of grief, or a frequent urge to weep that cannot be controlled. Seen in heart-spleen qi binding pattern, lung qi deficiency pattern, or visceral agitation (zangzao) and stroke. Also known as proneness to grief with desire to weep.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>喜悲伤欲哭</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
  
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
