    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/f#cat_睡眠类"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/f#PsychiatricFinding"/>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">舌体蜷缩，紧缩，不能伸长，严重者舌不抵齿，多为病情危重的征象。见于寒凝经脉证、气血虚衰证、热病伤津证、风痰阻络证等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">The tongue body is curled and contracted, unable to be extended; in severe cases it cannot reach the teeth—mostly a sign of critical illness. Seen in cold congealing in the channels pattern, qi-blood debilitation pattern, febrile disease damaging fluids pattern, or wind-phlegm obstructing the collaterals pattern.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.2.1.44</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度至中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>持续性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>环境刺激</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>饮食调整</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_舌短缩</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>The tongue body is curled and contracted, unable to be extended; in severe cases it cannot reach the teeth—mostly a sign of critical illness. Seen in cold congealing in the channels pattern, qi-blood debilitation pattern, febrile disease damaging fluids pattern, or wind-phlegm obstructing the collaterals pattern.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  
