    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">瘿肿随吞咽上下移动。见于痰气郁结证、痰瘀互结证、肝经火旺证、心肝阴虚证、心肾阴虚证、肝肾阴虚阳亢证，或气瘿、肉瘿、瘿气等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">The goiter moves up and down with swallowing. Seen in phlegm-qi stagnation pattern, phlegm-stasis intermingling pattern, liver channel fire exuberance pattern, heart-liver yin deficiency pattern, heart-kidney yin deficiency pattern, liver-kidney yin deficiency with yang hyperactivity pattern, or qi goiter, flesh goiter, or goiter qi disorder.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.6.3.28</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>重度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>持续性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>饮食不当</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>药物治疗</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:icd11>SF50</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Liver yin deficiency pattern (TM1)</tcm:icd11Term>
    <tcm:icd11>SF64</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Heart yin deficiency pattern (TM1)</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_瘿肿随吞咽移动</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
