    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/f#PsychiatricFinding"/>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">肛门排气多，声音响亮。见于肠道气滞证、肝旺脾虚证、肝胆气滞证、食滞胃肠证、胃肠湿热证、肝脾瘀滞证、脾虚营亏证、肝胃不和证，或肠郁、食亦、伤食、积滞、胆胀、胆石、脾痿、肥气、胃疡、大瘕泄、气腹痛等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Frequent loud flatus from the anus. Seen in intestinal qi stagnation pattern, liver exuberance with spleen deficiency pattern, liver-gallbladder qi stagnation pattern, food stagnating in the stomach and intestines pattern, gastrointestinal dampness-heat pattern, liver-spleen stasis pattern, spleen deficiency with nutrient depletion pattern, liver-stomach disharmony pattern, or intestinal depression (irritable bowel), food-also (excessive hunger), food damage, accumulation-stagnation, gallbladder distension, gallstones, spleen atrophy, fat qi (feiqi), stomach ulcer, great aggregation diarrhea, or qi abdominal pain.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.3.1.21</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>偶尔发作</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>饮食不当</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>情绪调节</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:icd11>SF72</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Spleen deficiency with qi stagnation pattern (TM1)</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_矢气作响</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Frequent loud flatus from the anus. Seen in intestinal qi stagnation pattern, liver exuberance with spleen deficiency pattern, liver-gallbladder qi stagnation pattern, food stagnating in the stomach and intestines pattern, gastrointestinal dampness-heat pattern, liver-spleen stasis pattern, spleen deficiency with nutrient depletion pattern, liver-stomach disharmony pattern, or intestinal depression (irritable bowel), food-also (excessive hunger), food damage, accumulation-stagnation, gallbladder distension, gallstones, spleen atrophy, fat qi (feiqi), stomach ulcer, great aggregation diarrhea, or qi abdominal pain.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ICD11:SF72</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
  
