      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">耳壳局部皮色不变，按之柔软，不热不痛，破溃流出黏液，易复发。见于水湿侵耳证、风热犯耳证、肝火犯耳证、邪恋耳窍证、痰凝耳窍证，或耳疖、耳疮、旋耳疮、脓耳等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">A local lesion of the auricle with unchanged skin color, soft on pressure, neither hot nor painful, discharging mucus after ulceration and prone to recurrence. Seen in water-dampness invading the ear pattern, wind-heat invading the ear pattern, liver fire invading the ear pattern, lingering pathogen in the ear orifice pattern, phlegm congealing in the ear orifice pattern, or ear furuncle, ear sore, circumrotating ear sore, or suppurative ear.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.6.10.2.20</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>重度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>每日多次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>感染、过敏</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>情绪调节</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_耳壳流痰</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A local lesion of the auricle with unchanged skin color, soft on pressure, neither hot nor painful, discharging mucus after ulceration and prone to recurrence. Seen in water-dampness invading the ear pattern, wind-heat invading the ear pattern, liver fire invading the ear pattern, lingering pathogen in the ear orifice pattern, phlegm congealing in the ear orifice pattern, or ear furuncle, ear sore, circumrotating ear sore, or suppurative ear.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  
