    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">忧思与焦虑并见，思绪无穷，不可自拔。见于肝气郁结证、痰气郁结证、气血瘀滞证、心神不宁证、心脾两虚证、心阴亏虚证、肝阴亏虚证，或癫病、癫狂病、脏躁、百合病、痫病等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Worry and anxiety occurring together, with endless thoughts from which one cannot extricate oneself. Seen in liver qi depression pattern, phlegm-qi stagnation pattern, qi-blood stasis pattern, heart-spirit restlessness pattern, heart-spleen dual deficiency pattern, heart yin deficiency pattern, liver yin deficiency pattern, or depressive psychosis (dian), dian-kuang psychosis, visceral agitation, lily disease, or epilepsy.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.4.1.6</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度至中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>间歇性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>环境刺激</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>休息、保暖</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:icd11>SF64</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Heart yin deficiency pattern (TM1)</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_思虑无穷</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Worry and anxiety occurring together, with endless thoughts from which one cannot extricate oneself. Seen in liver qi depression pattern, phlegm-qi stagnation pattern, qi-blood stasis pattern, heart-spirit restlessness pattern, heart-spleen dual deficiency pattern, heart yin deficiency pattern, liver yin deficiency pattern, or depressive psychosis (dian), dian-kuang psychosis, visceral agitation, lily disease, or epilepsy.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ICD11:SF64</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
  
