    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Stomach qi ascending counterflow, with qi seeming to rush up in the throat producing hiccup sounds beyond self-control. Seen in spleen-stomach qi deficiency pattern, or phlegm-qi obstructing the diaphragm pattern. Hiccup results from diaphragmatic spasm; also called yue.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>哕</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
