    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">脉来急促，一息五到六至（每分钟90次以上）。见于外感邪热、胃热证、阴虚证，或肠热下痢、肺痿、肺痈、宿食、疮疡、肠痈、狐蜮、百合病、虚劳等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">A rapid pulse, five to six beats per breath (over 90 beats per minute). Seen in externally contracted pathogenic heat, stomach heat pattern, yin deficiency pattern, or intestinal heat diarrhea, lung atrophy, lung abscess, retained food, sores/ulcers, intestinal abscess (appendicitis), gu-corpse disease (huyu), lily disease, or deficiency-taxation.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.2.2.8</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>持续性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>感染、过敏</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>药物治疗</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_脉数</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A rapid pulse, five to six beats per breath (over 90 beats per minute). Seen in externally contracted pathogenic heat, stomach heat pattern, yin deficiency pattern, or intestinal heat diarrhea, lung atrophy, lung abscess, retained food, sores/ulcers, intestinal abscess (appendicitis), gu-corpse disease (huyu), lily disease, or deficiency-taxation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
