    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">表情或动作迟饨，不灵敏。见于瘀阻脑络证、痰气郁结证、心脾两虚证，或癫病、癫痫病、痴呆等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Dull, slow expression or movements, lacking responsiveness. Seen in stasis obstructing the brain collaterals pattern, phlegm-qi stagnation pattern, heart-spleen dual deficiency pattern, or depressive psychosis (dian), epilepsy, or dementia.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.4.1.33</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度至中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>数小时一次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>环境刺激</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>饮食调整</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0000338</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:snomedCT>248149005</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>decreased facial expressions</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_神情呆滞</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Dull, slow expression or movements, lacking responsiveness. Seen in stasis obstructing the brain collaterals pattern, phlegm-qi stagnation pattern, heart-spleen dual deficiency pattern, or depressive psychosis (dian), epilepsy, or dementia.</obo:IAO_0000115>
