    <obo:IAO_0000115>Feces retained too long in the intestines, dry and hard with difficult evacuation, or infrequent defecation—usually no stool for two or three days or more. Seen in intestinal qi stagnation pattern, intestinal heat with bowel excess pattern, spleen-lung qi deficiency pattern, spleen-kidney yang deficiency pattern, cold stagnating in the intestines pattern, yin deficiency with intestinal dryness pattern, blood deficiency with intestinal dryness pattern, or intestinal impediment, spleen constraint (piyue), intestinal binding, intestinal cancer, lead poisoning, or intestinal depression. Also known as constipation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
