    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">脉在筋骨之间，如指弹石，辟辟凑指，毫无柔和软缓之象。见于肾水枯竭、风火内燔、亡阴。为无胃之脉。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">A pulse between the sinews and bones, like a finger flicking a stone—hard, urgent beats under the finger without any softness or gentleness. Seen in exhaustion of kidney water, internal blazing of wind-fire, or yin collapse; a pulse devoid of stomach qi.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.2.2.25</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度</tcm:severityText>
