      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/f#cat_睡眠类"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/f#PsychiatricFinding"/>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">视物昏花旋转，如坐舟车，严重者张目即觉旋地转，不能站立，或伴胸中上泛呕恶，甚或仆倒。见于肝阳上亢证、心脾气血两虚证、脾气虚证、肾精亏虚证、痰湿内阻证、瘀血阻络证，或风眩、脑络痹、虚眩、耳眩晕、子眩、子痈、产后出血晕、晕动病、脑痿、神劳、头部内伤、项痹、药物中毒、脑瘤等。又称头晕目眩。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Dizzy, blurred, spinning vision as if riding a boat or carriage; in severe cases the world spins upon opening the eyes, with inability to stand, accompanied by upwelling nausea in the chest, or even falling. Seen in liver yang hyperactivity pattern, heart-spleen qi-blood dual deficiency pattern, spleen qi deficiency pattern, kidney essence deficiency pattern, phlegm-dampness internal obstruction pattern, static blood obstructing the collaterals pattern, or wind dizziness (hypertension), brain collateral impediment, deficiency dizziness, ear vertigo, pregnancy dizziness (zixuan), pregnancy abscess (ziyong), postpartum hemorrhage syncope, motion sickness, brain atrophy, spirit taxation, internal head injury, nape impediment, drug poisoning, or brain tumor. Also known as dizziness with blurred vision.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.5.1.19</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:synonym>头晕目眩</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:synonym>眩晕</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0002321</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度至中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>持续性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>受凉、劳累</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>休息、保暖</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:snomedCT>399153001</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>Dizziness</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:icd11>MB48</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Dizziness and giddiness</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_头晕</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Dizzy, blurred, spinning vision as if riding a boat or carriage; in severe cases the world spins upon opening the eyes, with inability to stand, accompanied by upwelling nausea in the chest, or even falling. Seen in liver yang hyperactivity pattern, heart-spleen qi-blood dual deficiency pattern, spleen qi deficiency pattern, kidney essence deficiency pattern, phlegm-dampness internal obstruction pattern, static blood obstructing the collaterals pattern, or wind dizziness (hypertension), brain collateral impediment, deficiency dizziness, ear vertigo, pregnancy dizziness (zixuan), pregnancy abscess (ziyong), postpartum hemorrhage syncope, motion sickness, brain atrophy, spirit taxation, internal head injury, nape impediment, drug poisoning, or brain tumor. Also known as dizziness with blurred vision.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>头晕目眩</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>眩晕</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
