    <obo:IAO_0000115>Bleeding from one or both nasal passages (epistaxis). Seen in wind-cold attacking the nose pattern, wind-heat invading the nose pattern, dryness damaging the nasal orifices pattern, lung heat fuming the nose pattern, stomach heat fuming the nose pattern, liver fire invading the nose pattern, heart fire invading the nose pattern, depressed heat fuming the nose pattern, yin deficiency with unmoistened nasal orifices pattern, spleen deficiency with lung dryness pattern, spleen failing to govern blood pattern, or spleen-kidney yang deficiency pattern. Also known as nosebleed.</obo:IAO_0000115>
