    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">眼球突起，睑裂增大，甚至高突出眶。见于阴虚阳亢证、热毒炽盛证、痰瘀搏结证、气郁化火证，或鸪眼凝睛、眼内瘀血等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Protrusion of the eyeball with widened palpebral fissure, even bulging beyond the orbit (exophthalmos/proptosis). Seen in yin deficiency with yang hyperactivity pattern, heat toxin blazing pattern, phlegm-stasis contending and binding pattern, qi depression transforming into fire pattern, or hawk-eye fixed eye (gu yan ning jing) and intraocular stasis blood.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.6.10.1.25</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>中度至重度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>间歇性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>环境刺激</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>药物治疗</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0000520</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:snomedCT>18265008</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>anterior bulging of the globe</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_眼突</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Protrusion of the eyeball with widened palpebral fissure, even bulging beyond the orbit (exophthalmos/proptosis). Seen in yin deficiency with yang hyperactivity pattern, heat toxin blazing pattern, phlegm-stasis contending and binding pattern, qi depression transforming into fire pattern, or hawk-eye fixed eye (gu yan ning jing) and intraocular stasis blood.</obo:IAO_0000115>
