      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
      <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="Nde85ae5cb1444060b27b8f3b3ffcc222">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/accompanies"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/f#ClinicalFinding"/>
      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">指脉动显现部位浅表，轻按即得，重按反减，举之有余，按之不足。见于外感表证，或风水、皮水、虚劳类疾病、肝积肿瘤、邪闭喘咳等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">The pulse is palpable at a superficial level: obtained with light pressure and diminished on heavy pressure—abundant when lifted, insufficient when pressed. Seen in externally contracted exterior patterns, or wind edema (fengshui), skin edema (pishui), deficiency-taxation diseases, liver accumulation tumors, or pathogen-blocked dyspnea-cough.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.2.2.43</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>间歇性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>受凉、劳累</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>药物治疗</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_脉浮</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>The pulse is palpable at a superficial level: obtained with light pressure and diminished on heavy pressure—abundant when lifted, insufficient when pressed. Seen in externally contracted exterior patterns, or wind edema (fengshui), skin edema (pishui), deficiency-taxation diseases, liver accumulation tumors, or pathogen-blocked dyspnea-cough.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
