    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">病眼外观正常，唯视物歪斜，形态失真。见于肝郁血滞证、脾失健运证、肝肾阴亏证等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">The affected eye looks normal externally, but objects appear skewed and distorted in shape (metamorphopsia). Seen in liver depression with blood stagnation pattern, spleen failing in transport pattern, or liver-kidney yin depletion pattern.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.6.1.35</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>数小时一次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>饮食不当</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>休息、保暖</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:snomedCT>42134006</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>metamorphopsia</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_视物变形</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>The affected eye looks normal externally, but objects appear skewed and distorted in shape (metamorphopsia). Seen in liver depression with blood stagnation pattern, spleen failing in transport pattern, or liver-kidney yin depletion pattern.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:42134006</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://snomed.info/id/42134006"/>
  
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
