    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">发热，一日内体温上升、下降波动在1℃以上，但不降到正常。见于热证邪正交争。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Fever with daily temperature fluctuations exceeding 1°C between rise and fall, without returning to normal (remittent fever). Seen in heat patterns during struggle between pathogenic and righteous qi.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.1.2.13</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>数小时一次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>环境过热</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>退热药物、休息</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:snomedCT>77957000</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>episodic fever</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:icd11>1C33</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Q fever</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_弛张热</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Fever with daily temperature fluctuations exceeding 1°C between rise and fall, without returning to normal (remittent fever). Seen in heat patterns during struggle between pathogenic and righteous qi.</obo:IAO_0000115>
