    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">智能低下，记忆、理解、判断力明显减退，神情呆滞，反应迟钝，寡言善忘，甚至生活不能自理。见于先天性痴呆、小儿痴呆、老年性痴呆、头部内伤、脑萎、脑络痹、缺血中风、出血中风、煤气中毒、脑痨、春温后遗、暑温后遗症、瘿劳、呆小病、黑疸、蝶疮流注、酒癖等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Low intelligence with marked decline of memory, comprehension and judgment, dull expression, slow reactions, taciturnity and forgetfulness, even inability for self-care (dementia). Seen in congenital dementia, childhood dementia, senile dementia, internal head injury, brain atrophy, brain collateral impediment, ischemic stroke, hemorrhagic stroke, carbon monoxide poisoning, brain consumption, spring warmth sequelae, summerheat warmth sequelae, goiter taxation, cretinism, black jaundice, butterfly-sore flowing note (SLE), or alcohol addiction.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.4.1.30</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>每日多次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>感染、过敏</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>情绪调节</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:snomedCT>52448006</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>dementia</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:snomedCT>230288001</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>semantic dementia</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:snomedCT>278857002</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>frontal lobe dementia</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:icd11>SD86</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Dementia disorder (TM1)</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_痴呆</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Low intelligence with marked decline of memory, comprehension and judgment, dull expression, slow reactions, taciturnity and forgetfulness, even inability for self-care (dementia). Seen in congenital dementia, childhood dementia, senile dementia, internal head injury, brain atrophy, brain collateral impediment, ischemic stroke, hemorrhagic stroke, carbon monoxide poisoning, brain consumption, spring warmth sequelae, summerheat warmth sequelae, goiter taxation, cretinism, black jaundice, butterfly-sore flowing note (SLE), or alcohol addiction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
