    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">张口舒气，或伴困倦欲睡，或虽不觉困倦，仍频频呵欠。见于阴盛阳衰、气虚证、阳虚证、痰浊证等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Yawning with open mouth and exhalation, either with drowsiness or, without feeling sleepy, yawning repeatedly. Seen in yin exuberance with yang debilitation, qi deficiency pattern, yang deficiency pattern, or phlegm-turbidity pattern.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.4.2.17</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>偶尔发作</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>饮食不当</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>情绪调节</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:icd11>MD11.D</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Yawning</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_呵欠</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Yawning with open mouth and exhalation, either with drowsiness or, without feeling sleepy, yawning repeatedly. Seen in yin exuberance with yang debilitation, qi deficiency pattern, yang deficiency pattern, or phlegm-turbidity pattern.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ICD11:MD11.D</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
  
