    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/f#PsychiatricFinding"/>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">气从胃中上逆，声音沉长，气随声出，常伴腔胀。见于食滞胃肠证、肝气犯胃证、脾胃气虚证，或胃缓、食瘕、胃络痛、胃疡、胃痞、胃胀、伤食、积滞、胃郁、脾痿等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Qi rising counterflow from the stomach with a deep, prolonged sound as the gas is expelled, often accompanied by epigastric distension (belching). Seen in food stagnating in the stomach and intestines pattern, liver qi invading the stomach pattern, spleen-stomach qi deficiency pattern, or stomach slack, food aggregation, stomach collateral pain, stomach ulcer, stomach stuffiness, stomach distension, food damage, accumulation-stagnation, stomach depression, or spleen atrophy.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.3.1.50</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0100247</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:severityText>重度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>持续性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>受凉、劳累</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>休息、保暖</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:snomedCT>271824005</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>Belching</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:icd11>MD95</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Other specified symptoms of digestive system</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_嗳气</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Qi rising counterflow from the stomach with a deep, prolonged sound as the gas is expelled, often accompanied by epigastric distension (belching). Seen in food stagnating in the stomach and intestines pattern, liver qi invading the stomach pattern, spleen-stomach qi deficiency pattern, or stomach slack, food aggregation, stomach collateral pain, stomach ulcer, stomach stuffiness, stomach distension, food damage, accumulation-stagnation, stomach depression, or spleen atrophy.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>HPO:HP:0100247</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
