      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">自觉双下肢寒冷，可伴有喜暖。见于阳虚或经脉气血循行不畅（血痹）、热厥等证。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Subjective coldness of both lower limbs, possibly with a preference for warmth. Seen in yang deficiency, impeded qi-blood circulation in the channels (blood impediment), or heat syncope patterns.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.1.1.3</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>每日多次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>饮食不当</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>休息、保暖</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0033850</tcm:hpoID>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_下肢冷</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Subjective coldness of both lower limbs, possibly with a preference for warmth. Seen in yang deficiency, impeded qi-blood circulation in the channels (blood impediment), or heat syncope patterns.</obo:IAO_0000115>
