    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">无故喜乐，或嬉笑不休。见于肾水亏虚证、火热扰心证、痰热扰心证、心气惮乱证，或癫狂等。又称善喜，喜笑不休。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Groundless mirth or incessant laughing and giggling. Seen in kidney water deficiency pattern, fire-heat harassing the heart pattern, phlegm-heat harassing the heart pattern, heart qi trepidation pattern, or dian-kuang psychosis. Also known as proneness to laughing.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.4.1.5</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:synonym>善喜，喜笑不休</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>持续性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>受凉、劳累</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>休息、保暖</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0000748</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:snomedCT>247985007</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>inappropriate laughter</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_嬉笑无常</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Groundless mirth or incessant laughing and giggling. Seen in kidney water deficiency pattern, fire-heat harassing the heart pattern, phlegm-heat harassing the heart pattern, heart qi trepidation pattern, or dian-kuang psychosis. Also known as proneness to laughing.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>善喜，喜笑不休</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>HPO:HP:0000748</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
