    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">患者在安静状态下出现颈侧人迎脉怒张，平卧时更甚，或兼有搏动。见于心血瘀阻证、肺气壅滞证、心肾阳虚证、水气凌心证等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Distension of the renying (carotid) vessels on the side of the neck at rest, worse when lying flat, sometimes with visible pulsation. Seen in heart blood stasis obstruction pattern, lung qi congestion pattern, heart-kidney yang deficiency pattern, or water qi intimidating the heart pattern.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.6.3.6</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>每日多次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>感染、过敏</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>情绪调节</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_颈脉怒张</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Distension of the renying (carotid) vessels on the side of the neck at rest, worse when lying flat, sometimes with visible pulsation. Seen in heart blood stasis obstruction pattern, lung qi congestion pattern, heart-kidney yang deficiency pattern, or water qi intimidating the heart pattern.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
      <owl:Restriction>
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/dueTo"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/e#StasisEvil"/>
      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
  </owl:Class>
