    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">体温超过正常，或自觉有热感。又称身热。见于热证、外感疾病、阴虚、瘀阻、蕴毒等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Body temperature above normal, or a subjective sensation of heat. Also known as body heat. Seen in heat patterns, exogenous diseases, yin deficiency, stasis obstruction, or accumulated toxin.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.1.2.15</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:synonym>身热</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0001945</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:severityText>体温38-40℃</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>偶尔发作</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:reliefText>退热药物、休息</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:snomedCT>386661006</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>Fever</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:icd11>MG26</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Fever of other or unknown origin</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_发热</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Body temperature above normal, or a subjective sensation of heat. Also known as body heat. Seen in heat patterns, exogenous diseases, yin deficiency, stasis obstruction, or accumulated toxin.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>身热</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
