    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">头的额部前凸，颞部向两侧凸出，头顶部扁平，头部呈方形。见于先天肾精不足、脾胃失调证，或佝偻病、胎传梅毒等。又称头方。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">The forehead bulges forward, the temporal regions bulge bilaterally, and the vertex is flat, giving the head a square shape. Seen in congenital kidney essence insufficiency, spleen-stomach disorder pattern, or rickets and congenital syphilis. Also known as square head.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.6.8.1.33</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:synonym>头方</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:severityText>重度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>数小时一次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>情绪波动</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>饮食调整</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_方颅</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>The forehead bulges forward, the temporal regions bulge bilaterally, and the vertex is flat, giving the head a square shape. Seen in congenital kidney essence insufficiency, spleen-stomach disorder pattern, or rickets and congenital syphilis. Also known as square head.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>头方</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
  </owl:Class>
