    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">有声无痰谓之咳，有痰无声谓之嗽。见于风寒束表证、风热袭肺证、燥邪伤肺证、肺气虚证、肺阴虚证、肾阳虚证、肝火犯肺证、风痰恋肺证、痰热壅肺证、痰湿蕴肺证、寒饮停肺证，或暴咳、久咳、肺热病、哮病、肺痿、肺胀、肺络张、肺痨、肺癌、百日咳、尘肺、肺衰、肺厥、肺水、悬饮、气胸、肺虫病等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Sound without phlegm is called ke; phlegm without sound is called sou. Seen in wind-cold binding the exterior pattern, wind-heat invading the lung pattern, dryness pathogen damaging the lung pattern, lung qi deficiency pattern, lung yin deficiency pattern, kidney yang deficiency pattern, liver fire invading the lung pattern, wind-phlegm lingering in the lung pattern, phlegm-heat congesting the lung pattern, phlegm-dampness accumulating in the lung pattern, cold rheum collecting in the lung pattern, or sudden cough, chronic cough, lung heat disease, wheezing disease, lung atrophy, lung distension, lung collateral dilatation (bronchiectasis), lung consumption (tuberculosis), lung cancer, whooping cough, pneumoconiosis, lung failure, lung syncope, lung water, suspending rheum, pneumothorax, or lung worm disease.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.3.1.56</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0012735</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:frequencyText>每日多次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:snomedCT>49727002</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>Cough</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:icd11>MD12</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Cough</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_咳嗽</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Sound without phlegm is called ke; phlegm without sound is called sou. Seen in wind-cold binding the exterior pattern, wind-heat invading the lung pattern, dryness pathogen damaging the lung pattern, lung qi deficiency pattern, lung yin deficiency pattern, kidney yang deficiency pattern, liver fire invading the lung pattern, wind-phlegm lingering in the lung pattern, phlegm-heat congesting the lung pattern, phlegm-dampness accumulating in the lung pattern, cold rheum collecting in the lung pattern, or sudden cough, chronic cough, lung heat disease, wheezing disease, lung atrophy, lung distension, lung collateral dilatation (bronchiectasis), lung consumption (tuberculosis), lung cancer, whooping cough, pneumoconiosis, lung failure, lung syncope, lung water, suspending rheum, pneumothorax, or lung worm disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
