    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">上睑抬举无力或不能抬起以致睑裂变窄，甚至遮掩部分或全部瞳神，影响视物。见于气血两虚证、风痰阻络证、脾肾两虚证，或重症肌无力等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">The upper eyelid lifts weakly or cannot be raised, narrowing the palpebral fissure, even covering part or all of the pupil and impairing vision (ptosis). Seen in dual deficiency of qi and blood pattern, wind-phlegm obstructing the collaterals pattern, spleen-kidney dual deficiency pattern, or myasthenia gravis.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.6.10.1.55</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>间歇性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>环境刺激</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>休息、保暖</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:snomedCT>11934000</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>blepharoptosis</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:snomedCT>246815009</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>baggy eyes</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:snomedCT>268163008</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>congenital drooping upper eyelid</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
    <tcm:icd11>SK6L</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Ptosis disorder (TM2)</tcm:icd11Term>
    <tcm:icd11>LA14.04</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Congenital ptosis</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_眼睑下垂</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
