    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">指一侧或两侧目珠胀痛不适。见于阴虚血瘀证、阴虚阳亢证、火毒炽盛证、水轮气滞血瘀证，或突起睛高、物伤睛突、珠突出眶等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Distending pain and discomfort of one or both eyeballs. Seen in yin deficiency with blood stasis pattern, yin deficiency with yang hyperactivity pattern, fire toxin blazing pattern, water-wheel qi stagnation with blood stasis pattern, or protruding raised eye (acute proptosis), object-injured protruding eye, or eyeball protruding beyond the orbit.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.6.1.26</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度至中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>持续性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>饮食不当</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>饮食调整</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_目胀</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Distending pain and discomfort of one or both eyeballs. Seen in yin deficiency with blood stasis pattern, yin deficiency with yang hyperactivity pattern, fire toxin blazing pattern, water-wheel qi stagnation with blood stasis pattern, or protruding raised eye (acute proptosis), object-injured protruding eye, or eyeball protruding beyond the orbit.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  
