    <obo:IAO_0000115>Inability to see distant or near objects clearly. Seen in liver-kidney deficiency pattern, primal yang deficiency pattern, or eye diseases such as crescent-moon invading the eye (pterygium), flowery nebula with white sinking, congealed-fat nebula (suppurative keratitis), yellow fluid rushing upward (hypopyon), spiral bulge, black nebula like a pearl, pupil diseases, orthorrhea (fistula leakage), mixed-eye opacity, drooping red membrane (pannus), blood nebula enveloping the eye, or chronic nebula (corneal scar).</obo:IAO_0000115>
