    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">肛门排气频繁，多有声。见于肝胆气滞证、食滞胃肠证、肝旺脾虚证、胃肠湿热证，或肠郁、食亦、脾痿、大瘕泄等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Frequent passage of flatus from the anus, mostly audible. Seen in liver-gallbladder qi stagnation pattern, food stagnating in the stomach and intestines pattern, liver exuberance with spleen deficiency pattern, gastrointestinal dampness-heat pattern, or intestinal depression, food-also, spleen atrophy, or great aggregation diarrhea.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.3.1.34</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度至中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>偶尔发作</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>感染、过敏</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>情绪调节</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_矢气频作</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Frequent passage of flatus from the anus, mostly audible. Seen in liver-gallbladder qi stagnation pattern, food stagnating in the stomach and intestines pattern, liver exuberance with spleen deficiency pattern, gastrointestinal dampness-heat pattern, or intestinal depression, food-also, spleen atrophy, or great aggregation diarrhea.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  
