    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">无故发怒，或易于发怒，情绪急躁不能自制。见于肝郁气滞证、肝胆火旺证、肝脾不调证、肝肾阴虚证，或神劳、癫病、狂病、风眩、瘿气、经行情志异常、子烦、绝经前后诸症等。烦躁易怒可并见，见于肠热腑实证、阴虚火旺证、余热内扰证、心肾不交证、阴盛格阳证，或中暑、神劳、神郁、脏躁、狂病、癫病、百合病、头部内伤、子烦、经行情志异常、绝经前后诸症、疳积、佝偻病、夏季热、风眩、瘿气等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Groundless anger, or being easily angered, with irritability beyond self-control. Seen in liver depression with qi stagnation pattern, liver-gallbladder fire exuberance pattern, liver-spleen disharmony pattern, liver-kidney yin deficiency pattern, or spirit taxation, depressive psychosis (dian), manic psychosis (kuang), wind dizziness, goiter qi disorder, menstrual emotional disorders, pregnancy vexation (zifan), or perimenopausal syndrome. When co-occurring with vexation it is seen in intestinal heat with bowel excess pattern, yin deficiency with effulgent fire pattern, residual heat internal harassment pattern, heart-kidney non-interaction pattern, yin exuberance repelling yang pattern, or heatstroke, spirit taxation, spirit depression, visceral agitation, manic psychosis, depressive psychosis, lily disease, internal head injury, pregnancy vexation, menstrual emotional disorders, perimenopausal syndrome, infantile malnutrition, rickets, summer fever, wind dizziness, or goiter qi disorder.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.4.1.37</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度至中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>间歇性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>受凉、劳累</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>药物治疗</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:icd11>MB24.C</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Irritability</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_易怒</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Groundless anger, or being easily angered, with irritability beyond self-control. Seen in liver depression with qi stagnation pattern, liver-gallbladder fire exuberance pattern, liver-spleen disharmony pattern, liver-kidney yin deficiency pattern, or spirit taxation, depressive psychosis (dian), manic psychosis (kuang), wind dizziness, goiter qi disorder, menstrual emotional disorders, pregnancy vexation (zifan), or perimenopausal syndrome. When co-occurring with vexation it is seen in intestinal heat with bowel excess pattern, yin deficiency with effulgent fire pattern, residual heat internal harassment pattern, heart-kidney non-interaction pattern, yin exuberance repelling yang pattern, or heatstroke, spirit taxation, spirit depression, visceral agitation, manic psychosis, depressive psychosis, lily disease, internal head injury, pregnancy vexation, menstrual emotional disorders, perimenopausal syndrome, infantile malnutrition, rickets, summer fever, wind dizziness, or goiter qi disorder.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ICD11:MB24.C</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
  
