    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">脉在皮肤，来则隐隐其形，时而跃然而去，如虾游冉冉，忽而一跃的状态。见于阴绝阳败。为无根脉。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">A pulse in the skin, faint on arrival, then darting away—like a shrimp swimming and suddenly leaping. Seen in yin exhaustion and yang defeat; a rootless pulse.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.2.2.18</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>重度</tcm:severityText>
