    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">饮食乏味，或没有食欲，或虽能进食，但不知食物味道。见于肝气犯胃证、脾胃湿热证、脾胃气虚证、脾胃虚寒证、脾肾阳虚证，或伤食、鼻咽口腔疾病、外感病等。可与口淡乏味并见。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Food tastes dull, or there is no appetite, or the patient can eat but cannot taste the food. Seen in liver qi invading the stomach pattern, spleen-stomach dampness-heat pattern, spleen-stomach qi deficiency pattern, spleen-stomach deficiency cold pattern, spleen-kidney yang deficiency pattern, or food damage, nasopharyngeal/oral diseases, or exogenous diseases. May co-occur with bland tastelessness in the mouth.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.1.3.43</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0004396</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:severityText>轻度至中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>间歇性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>情绪波动</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>饮食调整</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:snomedCT>64379006</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>decreased appetite</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_纳谷不馨</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Food tastes dull, or there is no appetite, or the patient can eat but cannot taste the food. Seen in liver qi invading the stomach pattern, spleen-stomach dampness-heat pattern, spleen-stomach qi deficiency pattern, spleen-stomach deficiency cold pattern, spleen-kidney yang deficiency pattern, or food damage, nasopharyngeal/oral diseases, or exogenous diseases. May co-occur with bland tastelessness in the mouth.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>HPO:HP:0004396</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
