    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">头部不自觉地摇动或摇摆不能自制。见于肝阳上亢证、阴虚动风证、气血两虚证等。又称摇头风。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Involuntary shaking or swaying of the head beyond self-control. Seen in liver yang hyperactivity pattern, yin deficiency stirring wind pattern, or dual deficiency of qi and blood pattern. Also known as head-shaking wind.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.6.8.1.8</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:synonym>摇头风</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:hpoID>HP:0002346</tcm:hpoID>
    <tcm:severityText>重度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>持续性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>环境刺激</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>饮食调整</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_头摇</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Involuntary shaking or swaying of the head beyond self-control. Seen in liver yang hyperactivity pattern, yin deficiency stirring wind pattern, or dual deficiency of qi and blood pattern. Also known as head-shaking wind.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>摇头风</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>HPO:HP:0002346</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
