    </rdfs:subClassOf>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">脉来一息四至，稍快于迟脉，脉来从容和缓为平缓脉，来去怠缓无力，或兼迟细或兼滑大则为病脉。见于脾气虚证、虚寒证，或气血两虚证、湿阻阳遏证等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">A pulse of four beats per breath, slightly faster than the slow pulse: when leisurely, harmonious and moderate it is a normal moderate pulse; when sluggish, weak, or combined with slow-thin or slippery-large qualities it is a morbid pulse. Seen in spleen qi deficiency pattern, deficiency cold pattern, dual deficiency of qi and blood pattern, or dampness obstructing with yang repressed pattern.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.2.2.36</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>重度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>每日多次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>受凉、劳累</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>药物治疗</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:icd11>XS0T</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Moderate</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_脉缓</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A pulse of four beats per breath, slightly faster than the slow pulse: when leisurely, harmonious and moderate it is a normal moderate pulse; when sluggish, weak, or combined with slow-thin or slippery-large qualities it is a morbid pulse. Seen in spleen qi deficiency pattern, deficiency cold pattern, dual deficiency of qi and blood pattern, or dampness obstructing with yang repressed pattern.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ICD11:XS0T</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
  
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
      <owl:Restriction>
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/dueTo"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/tcm_v38/e#DampnessEvil"/>
      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
  </owl:Class>
