    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">可触及内躁之后太溪穴处的动脉搏动。为正常，提示足府幼脉供血正常。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">The arterial pulsation at the Taixi point behind the medial malleolus is palpable—normal, indicating normal blood supply of the foot-shaoyin vessel.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.2.2.15</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>中度至重度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>持续性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>环境刺激</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>情绪调节</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_太溪脉在</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>The arterial pulsation at the Taixi point behind the medial malleolus is palpable—normal, indicating normal blood supply of the foot-shaoyin vessel.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  </owl:Class>
