    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">眼眦部长出大片红肉，其状如蝇翅，横贯白睛，向黑睛攀入，甚则遮盖瞳神。见于风热壅盛证、脾胃实热证、心火上炎证、三焦壅热证、阴虚火旺证等。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">A large patch of red flesh growing from the canthus, shaped like a fly's wing, crossing the white of the eye and climbing into the cornea, even covering the pupil (pterygium). Seen in wind-heat congestion pattern, spleen-stomach excess heat pattern, heart fire flaming upward pattern, triple-jiao congested heat pattern, or yin deficiency with effulgent fire pattern.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.6.10.1.110</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>间歇性</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>环境刺激</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>休息、保暖</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_胬肉攀睛</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A large patch of red flesh growing from the canthus, shaped like a fly's wing, crossing the white of the eye and climbing into the cornea, even covering the pupil (pterygium). Seen in wind-heat congestion pattern, spleen-stomach excess heat pattern, heart fire flaming upward pattern, triple-jiao congested heat pattern, or yin deficiency with effulgent fire pattern.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  
