    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">迎风则泪流无法控制。见于肝血虚证，或椒疮等。又称迎风流泪。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Uncontrollable tearing when facing the wind. Seen in liver blood deficiency pattern, or pepper sore (trachoma). Also known as tearing against the wind.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.6.10.1.15</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:synonym>迎风流泪</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:severityText>中度至重度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>每日多次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>情绪波动</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>药物治疗</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:icd11>SF54</tcm:icd11>
    <tcm:icd11Term>Liver blood deficiency pattern (TM1)</tcm:icd11Term>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_遇风流泪</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Uncontrollable tearing when facing the wind. Seen in liver blood deficiency pattern, or pepper sore (trachoma). Also known as tearing against the wind.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>迎风流泪</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ICD11:SF54</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
  </owl:Class>
