    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">脉在皮肤，头定而尾摇，似有似无，如鱼在水中游动。见于三阴寒极、亡阳证。为无根脉。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">A pulse in the skin, its head fixed and tail swaying, seeming present yet absent, like a fish swimming in water. Seen in extreme cold of the three yin, or yang collapse pattern; a rootless pulse.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.2.2.21</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:severityText>重度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>数小时一次</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>感染、过敏</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>休息、保暖</tcm:reliefText>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_鱼翔脉</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A pulse in the skin, its head fixed and tail swaying, seeming present yet absent, like a fish swimming in water. Seen in extreme cold of the three yin, or yang collapse pattern; a rootless pulse.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
