    <tcm:definition xml:lang="zh-cn">妇女行经时发生肢体抽搐，经后自愈。见于肝血不足、脾肾两虚证。又称经行肢体拘急。</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:definition xml:lang="en">Limb convulsions occurring during menstruation, resolving spontaneously afterward. Seen in liver blood insufficiency, or spleen-kidney dual deficiency pattern. Also known as menstrual limb contracture.</tcm:definition>
    <tcm:reference>Book(中医临床常见症状术语规范)、 8.5.2.2.71</tcm:reference>
    <tcm:synonym>经行肢体拘急</tcm:synonym>
    <tcm:severityText>中度</tcm:severityText>
    <tcm:frequencyText>偶尔发作</tcm:frequencyText>
    <tcm:triggerText>环境刺激</tcm:triggerText>
    <tcm:reliefText>情绪调节</tcm:reliefText>
    <tcm:snomedCT>386692008</tcm:snomedCT>
    <tcm:snomedCTTerm>abnormally heavy bleeding during menstruation</tcm:snomedCTTerm>
  
    <oboInOwl:id>TCM-SO:sx_经行抽搐</oboInOwl:id>
    <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>TCM_symptom</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Limb convulsions occurring during menstruation, resolving spontaneously afterward. Seen in liver blood insufficiency, or spleen-kidney dual deficiency pattern. Also known as menstrual limb contracture.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>经行肢体拘急</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:386692008</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    <skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="http://snomed.info/id/386692008"/>
  </owl:Class>
